So `pushTab` is initially NULL. It only gets allocated in `nameNsPush` when `ctxt->nameNr >= ctxt->nameMax` OR when `ctxt->pushTab == NULL`. But `nameNsPush` is only called when `ctxt->sax2` is true. 

The key issue: In `xmlParseElement` at line 9962-9963, it accesses `ctxt->pushTab[ctxt->nameNr - 1].line` regardless of whether `sax2` is set. If `sax2` is false (SAX1 mode), `namePush` is used instead of `nameNsPush`, so `pushTab` remains NULL. Then accessing `ctxt->pushTab[ctxt->nameNr - 1].line` would be a NULL pointer dereference.

